Partial refunds must always be rounded down (floor) to the whole cent, never rounded to the nearest cent. This is a decision from finance.

**Why:** The payment provider rejects a refund that exceeds what is left of the captured amount. Rounding to nearest could round up, so the last of several partial refunds failed.

**How to apply:** Any code that computes a partial refund amount (proration, split refunds, etc.) must floor to the cent (e.g. integer minor units with floor division, or `ROUND_DOWN`/`floor`), not use round-half-up/half-even. No code change was requested at the time this was recorded (2026-11-26); apply it when touching refund logic.
